    "narrative": "The offensive centerpiece for the Austin Waves today is **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the lineup with a 76.60 score despite a challenging matchup against Woo. While the 3.42 xERA of the opposing starter provides a stiff test, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) and his prime position in the two-hole. **Kyle Tucker** (68.81) and **Andy Pages** (64.76) follow closely as our most reliable options; both capitalize on positive platoon splits against Keller and maintain strong efficiency metrics that make them near-auto-starts. **Josh Jung** (62.69) is also a strong play today, aided by a wind-out projection at the stadium that elevates his power ceiling beyond his base expectations.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved balancing the scarcity of stolen bases against daily efficiency. While **Sam Antonacci** (41.83) and **Coby Mayo** (42.53) both grade out as marginal starts, they are barely holding onto their spots due to unfavorable batting order positions (9th and 8th, respectively). **Liam Hicks** (59.92) is currently our strongest catcher play, benefiting from an elite-matchup bump (+19% SP skill adjustment) against Kelly. We are actively monitoring the 42% rain risk in the game involving **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; should that game be scrubbed, we will be forced to pivot to our thin bench, which remains compromised by the ongoing IL stints of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, as well as scheduled off-days for core pieces like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**.",
